     "larva",
     "tadpole",
     "stagnant"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A mosquito goes through egg, larva, pupa and adult. The eggs and larvae live in stagnant water, which is why we must not let water collect.\nA frog goes through egg, tadpole, young frog and adult frog. The tadpole breathes with gills and lives in water, and the adult breathes with lungs and skin.\nAnimals like birds and mammals have simpler cycles; their young look like small adults."
    }
